xnu: put the firmware cache image through the new context and light CM3 (0193)

With the context verified on hardware (bank 1, ASID 1, ttbr0 to our root, all
nine fields reading back identical), the two things 0187 had to skip can finally
be done for real:

  - region2 (0x4000 + 0xdcac) is copied into the data block through the same
    mapping the SMMU will translate, then cleaned to the PoC;
  - HFI_QTBL_ADDR and GENERAL_8 are programmed with the iovas that
    sweet_adreno_smmu_context() actually mapped (0x60008000 and 0x60004000|3),
    and read back so the log shows what the GMU will see.

Delayed work now runs the context first and the GMU load second: releasing CM3
before the translation exists is exactly what reset the machine twice.

This is the first configuration that can legitimately release CM3_SYSRESET; the
console ring is flushed immediately before that write, so a reset still leaves
the evidence on disk.
